[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818508059,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818694869,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818702929,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81870763,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818711687,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818716478,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81872471,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818728883,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818732817,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818737281,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818741166,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818843887,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer: noise simulations under a retained calibration export, design power analyses, parameter sweeps | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81885042,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818855023,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. Batch pushes requesting either ID ran on 4-core CPU machines without libtpu, so this account reaches no TPU through the CLI | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818860424,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818865458,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818869523000004,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818873764,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818878298,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818881966,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818885859,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818890182,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818894766,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818899288,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818903051,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818907433,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818911328,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818916046,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818922076,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818937162,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818941415,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818945434,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818949376,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818954016,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818958026,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818962962,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818966885,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818971106,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818974905,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81897871,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818982419,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818986913,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818990846,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818995514,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.818999558,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819004111,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819008529,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819012678,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819016701,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819020602,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81902472,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81902829,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.81903249,"data":"- A kernel is private, has GPU and internet enabled, and holds no IBM\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819036841,"data":"  credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819040862,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819044776,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE` and selects the GPU through it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819048672,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819052681,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819056604,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819061253,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819065927,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819070032,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819078648,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":45.819082945,"data":"\n"}
